# LCL layout and ChangeBounds stability

## What triggers loops

`TControl.ChangeBounds loop detected` means two layout owners fought in one cascade: manual `SetBounds`, LCL `Align`/`ReAlign`, and/or native control preferred size (especially `TComboBox`).

## Do not

- Mix **`Align` (especially `alClient`)** with manual **`SetBounds`** on the **same** control.
- Set **`TComboBox.Height`** in theme helpers (`StyleComboBox`) while another place (`UpdateLayout`, `.lfm`) sets a different height.
- Use ad-hoc combo heights (23, 24, 28) in panels; use **`uTheme`** constants or `EffectiveThemedComboBoxHeight`.
- Run layout from `Resize` without a **re-entrancy guard** (`FUpdatingLayout` / `FInLayout`) when the handler calls `SetBounds` on children.
- Manual `SetBounds(0, HeaderH, …)` on tab pages; use **`AdjustClientRect`** on the parent ([`uCustomTabControl.pas`](uCustomTabControl.pas)).

## Do

- **One geometry owner** per control: either LCL alignment **or** explicit manual layout, not both.
- Custom tab headers: override **`AdjustClientRect`**, active page **`Align := alClient`**, defer page layout until **`Loaded`** when streaming `.lfm`.
- Themed combos: **`StyleComboBox`** for colors/style/`ItemHeight` only; **caller** sets bounds using **`EffectiveThemedComboBoxHeight`** from `uTheme` (not ad-hoc pixel heights).
- Designer forms: stream **compatible** `Height`/`ItemHeight` on `TComboBox` in `.lfm` matching runtime theme metrics (`ThemedComboBoxHeight`, `ThemedComboBoxItemHeight`).
- After **reparent** (detach/attach in [`uDockPanel.pas`](uDockPanel.pas)): expect resize + theme; ensure `ApplyTheme` and layout order do not re-fight combo height.
- Verify: detach panel, resize, theme toggle — no ChangeBounds dialog.

